  "description": "The sentence spec/execution-model.md:597-601 adds to the block rule: \"a top-level `on_click [ :score = :score + 1 ]` needs no declaration: `:score` is a top-level name and the handler block is written at the top level\". Dropping the `global` from the sibling `a-global-counts-clicks-across-handler-firings` must therefore change nothing — the same two clicks still leave `2`. Pinned because the sealed boundary makes `global` look like the price of shared mutable state, and for a top-level handler it is not; requiring it here would be a regression the `global` fixture alone cannot see.",
